Package: coolercontrold
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, sparky-stereo-problems (>= 0.2.1)
Recommends: liquidctl, lm-sensors
Description: Cooling control and monitoring: the system service
 CoolerControl reads the temperatures and sets the fans, pumps and lights of a
 computer: the motherboard's and the processor's sensors and fan channels
 through the kernel's hwmon interface, graphics cards, and liquid coolers and
 fan controllers through liquidctl. This is its system service, with the web
 interface it serves (http://localhost:11987) and the programming interface
 the window uses. Profiles, functions, alerts and modes are kept in
 /etc/coolercontrol.
 .
 The package is built from the release's source: the daemon's Rust crates are
 vendored, and the interface is built with Vite 7, Rollup (its native part
 built from source) and Debian's esbuild, not with upstream's prebuilt
 bundler. A copy made by upstream's makefile (/usr/local) is left as it is.
 .
 Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's edition of SparkyLinux (by Pawel "pavroo"
 Pijanowski). Upstream: Guy Boldon, Eren Simsek and the CoolerControl contributors.

Package: coolercontrol
Architecture: amd64
Depends: coolercontrold (= ${binary:Version}), qt6-qpa-plugins, libqt6webenginecore6-bin, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Cooling control and monitoring: the desktop window
 The Qt window of CoolerControl: the interface of the service in a web view
 of its own, with a tray icon and desktop notifications for the alerts.
